# Rust build output
/target/
# The two external-consumer fixtures are SEPARATE WORKSPACES (deliberately: they
# may name only the SDK facade), so each builds its own multi-gigabyte target
# outside the root one above. ⛔ they are also outside the repository gate — see
# `fixtures/minimal_game/src/minimal_experience.rs` for the eight days that cost.
fixtures/*/target/
# `examples/capability_demo` and `examples/portal_tutorial` are separate
# workspaces for the same reason, and were missing from this list until the
# Bevy 0.19 port actually built them.
examples/*/target/

# Generated browser bundle (wasm-bindgen output from ./build_for_web.sh).
game/ambition_app/web/pkg/
# The composed asset tree `./build_for_web.sh --served` publishes (via
# scripts/package_asset_guard.py) so the served browser persona can fetch
# `/assets/...` over HTTP, plus the byte contract that publication proves.
game/ambition_app/web/assets
game/ambition_app/web/.assets_contract.json
game/ambition_app/web/.assets_sha256

