# ⛔⛔ THE SAME SIX PATHS AGAIN, WITHOUT THE TRAILING SLASH.
#
# A trailing slash matches a DIRECTORY ONLY. On 2026-08-20 all six of these were
# committed to main as SYMLINKS — directory links pointing at the main checkout's
# copy, made in a worktree, which check out in the main tree as links to
# themselves. `git check-ignore` reported them NOT IGNORED, so an ordinary
# `git add` took them and six ignore rules watched it happen.
#
# ⚠ a directory link here is a defect in its own right, not just an ignore
# escape: `scripts/mirror_assets_for_worktree.py` mirrors these trees FILE BY
# FILE on purpose, because "directory links would send that write straight into
# main's assets, which is exactly the accident this exists to prevent."
crates/ambition_platformer2d_actor_monolith/assets/audio
crates/ambition_platformer2d_actor_monolith/assets/fonts
crates/ambition_platformer2d_actor_monolith/assets/sprite_packs
crates/ambition_platformer2d_actor_monolith/assets/sprites_0_25x
crates/ambition_platformer2d_actor_monolith/assets/sprites_0_5x
crates/ambition_platformer2d_actor_monolith/assets/sprites_potato
crates/ambition_platformer2d_actor_monolith/assets/backgrounds/parallax_layers_0_5x/
crates/ambition_platformer2d_actor_monolith/assets/backgrounds/parallax_layers_0_25x/
crates/ambition_platformer2d_actor_monolith/assets/backgrounds/parallax_layers_potato/

# Agent/worktree scratch (must never be committed)
.worktrees/
# ⛔ BOTH SPELLINGS. This was `.tmp-ambition-agent-source-*/` only, and the
# handoff snapshots are actually named WITHOUT the `.tmp-` prefix — so the rule
# read as protection and had never matched anything. 11 files of a duplicate
# Mary-O sprite generator were tracked for three days behind it.
.tmp-ambition-agent-source-*/
ambition-agent-source-*/

coverage-reports/
untracked

# Repo-root scripts venv (tree-sitter for ecs_inventory etc.)
.venv/

# Armed goal state for scripts/goal_guard.py (per-run, never shared)
.goal/

# Zips dropped at the repo root. Standing rule: an overlay is never APPLIED — a
# change lands as reviewed edits or not at all — so these are inputs to read, not
# artifacts to track (and never binaries to commit).
#
# ⛔ this was `/*_overlay_*.zip`, matching UNDERSCORES, and every zip Jon has
# actually dropped here is hyphenated
# (`ambition-super-mary-o-quasar-buttons-overlay-20260802 (2).zip`). The rule
# never matched once. Nothing at the repo root is a zip that belongs in history,
# so the pattern is now the whole class rather than a guess at the name.
/*.zip

# Emulator artifacts dropped in the repo root by a REFERENCE session — an SM64
# config + save appeared here on 2026-07-28 while somebody was looking at what
# classic physics actually feels like. They are runtime state of another
# program, not project files: nothing here reads them, and one is a binary.
#
# Ignored rather than deleted. They belong to whoever ran the emulator, and a
# clean `git status` is not worth throwing away somebody's keybindings.
/sm64config.txt
/sm64_save_file.bin

# >>> llm_resource_tally local state (managed) >>>
/.llm_resource_tally/local/
# <<< llm_resource_tally local state (managed) <<<

# The compile-telemetry report — generated by `scripts/compile_report.py` from the
# five ledgers in `dev/ambition_dev_measurements/`, in well under a second. Tracking
# it would put a 236 KB diff in history every time a ledger gained a row, and the
# copy in the tree would be stale the moment one did. The LEDGERS are the record;
# this is a view of them, which is also why it stays in THIS repo rather than
# following the ledgers into the submodule.
/dev/compile_report.html

# Profiler output, dropped at the repository root by whichever run asked for it
# (`line_profiler`'s `.lprof` binary plus its rendered text, and the timestamped
# copies a comparison run leaves behind). A profile is a MEASUREMENT of one run
# on one machine — the thing worth keeping from it is the finding, which belongs
# in `dev/` where the engineering memory lives, not an 80 KB dump of line timings
# whose numbers mean nothing without the machine that produced them.
/profile_output.lprof
/profile_output.txt
/profile_output_*.txt

# The `cargo-sweep` mark file. `cargo sweep --stamp` writes it before a build
# and `cargo sweep --file` cleans everything older than it afterwards, which is
# how this checkout keeps a 484G target from filling. It is a TIMESTAMP of one
# build on one machine — the next agent to run the mark/sweep pair overwrites it,
# and a committed one would be a stale mark that sweeps a live working set.
/sweep.timestamp

git-of-theseus

# Machine-local launcher config (see ambition.local.toml.example).
# Describes ONE machine: what it can afford to draw and what it boots into.
ambition.local.toml
